# Visual identity and craft floor
System.Management.Automation.RemoteException
## Universal rules
System.Management.Automation.RemoteException
- The exact client brand and verified assets override global taste.
- Start with hierarchy, composition, typography, and contrast before animation.
- Avoid generic AI gradients, repeated rounded cards, excessive pills, template
  symmetry, decorative dashboards, and motion without narrative purpose.
- Use the Impeccable workflow for substantive UI work and retain `PRODUCT.md`
  plus `DESIGN.md` as project context.
- Verify responsive behavior, keyboard access, visible focus, reduced motion,
  text contrast, overflow, loading states, and the browser console.
- Client image generation requires a verified logo plus at least one approved
  client/product/style reference. A text prompt alone is insufficient.
- Generated visuals remain local review drafts until the exact delivery or
  publication gate is satisfied.
